  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "سَعْدٌ عَنْ أَيُّوبَ بْنِ نُوحٍ عَنْ صَفْوَانَ عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ مُسْكَانَ عَنِ الْحَسَنِ بْنِ زِيَادٍ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Sa'd narrated from Ayyub ibn Nuh from Safwan from Abdullah ibn Muskhan from al-Hasan ibn Ziyad from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him) who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "«هِيَ تَرِثُ وَ تُورَثُ مَا كَانَ لَهُ الرَّجْعَةُ بَيْنَ التَّطْلِيقَتَيْنِ الْأُولَتَيْنِ حَتَّى تَغْتَسِلَ». فَالْوَجْهُ فِي هَذَيْنِ الْخَبَرَيْنِ مَا قَدَّمْنَاهُ أَيْضاً مِنَ التَّقِيَّةِ وَ كَانَ شَيْخُنَا رَحِمَهُ اللَّهُ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَ هَذِهِ الْأَخْبَارِ بِأَنْ يَقُولَ إِذَا طَلَّقَهَا فِي آخِرِ طُهْرِهَا اعْتَدَّتْ بِالْحَيْضِ وَ إِنْ طَلَّقَهَا فِي أَوَّلِهِ اعْتَدَّتْ بِالْأَقْرَاءِ الَّتِي هِيَ الْأَطْهَارُ وَ هَذَا وَجْهٌ غَيْرَ أَنَّ الْأَوْلَى مَا قَدَّمْنَاهُ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "\"She inherits and is inherited from as long as he has the right of return between the first two divorces, until she performs the ritual bath.\" The view in these two narrations is what we previously mentioned, namely al-taqiyyah (dissimulation/prudence), and our Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) reconciles these narrations by saying: If he divorces her at the end of her purity (menses-free period), she observes the waiting period by counting her menses; and if he divorces her at its beginning, she observes the waiting period by counting the menstruations which are the pure ones. This is one view, although the preferred one is what we previously mentioned."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith discusses the legal status of a woman in a triple divorce scenario where the husband retains the right of return (raj'ah). It clarifies that she remains in the marital bond (inheriting and being inherited from) until she performs the ritual bath (ghusl) after the third divorce, and addresses the method of counting the waiting period (iddah) based on when the divorce occurred relative to her menstrual cycle.",
      "seo_question": "How is the waiting period (iddah) calculated for a woman divorced before consummation or during the purity phase, and when does the marital bond end?",
      "key_terms": {
        "الرَّجْعَةُ": "The right of return (revocation of divorce) during the waiting period",
        "التَّطْلِيقَتَيْنِ الْأُولَتَيْنِ": "The first two divorces in a triple divorce sequence",
        "تَغْتَسِلُ": "She performs the ritual bath (ghusl)",
        "الْحَيْضُ": "Menstruation",
        "الْأَقْرَاءُ": "Menstruation (specifically the pure periods used for counting iddah)",
        "الْdah in this context)"
